</div>

<p>The hospital contained 12 private rooms, ten double rooms, a large ward, and apartments for attendants and employees. Mandan's eight practicing physicians received initial privileges, and seven registered nurses staffed the facility. The third floor was initially expected to house a three-year nursing school.</p>

<p>Area Methodist churches assumed operation in 1918. The institution, renamed Deaconess Hospital, served patients of all faiths.</p>

<div class="image-gallery">
  <figure>
